# T9: an array remembers the kind of its items when it is empty, as
# APL2's prototype does: "" is an empty character vector, so DISPLAY
# marks it as characters (the plain bottom line), while an empty
# number vector keeps the numbers mark.
== SOURCE
d_isplay ""
d_isplay 0 r_eshape 1
s_hape ""
== TYPE
Char
Char
Int
== RESULT
┌⊖┐
│ │
└─┘
┌⊖┐
│ │
└~┘
0
